{"term":"sacrifice","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:8a029da3b583fee532","definition":"Originally, the killing (and often burning) of a human being or an animal as an offering to a deity; later, also the offering of an object to a deity.","example":"They firſt vvaſh the dead body, paint him, clothe him, and ſo conueigh him to his Dormitorie, vvhich is ſpacious and neat, vvherein they bury his Armolets, Bracelets, Shackles and ſuch Treaſure, concluding their Ceremonies vvith Mimmicke geſtures and eiaculations: vvhich, vvith the Sacrifice of a Goat, vpon his Graue, puts a period to their Burials.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["human sacrifice","nonsacrifice","presacrifice","pseudosacrifice","sac","sacrifice area","sacrifice bunt","sacrifice fly","sacrifice hit","sacrificeless","sacrifice zone","salary sacrifice","self-sacrifice","supreme sacrifice","ultimate sacrifice","resacrifice"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sacrifice#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:142c55770645c791eb","definition":"A human being or an animal, or a physical object or immaterial thing (see etymology 1 sense 1.3), offered to a deity.","example":"O th'inchaunting vvords of that baſe ſlaue, / Made him to thinke Epeus pine-tree Horſe [i.e., the Trojan Horse] / A ſacrifize t'appeaſe Mineruas vvrath: […]","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["human sacrifice","nonsacrifice","presacrifice","pseudosacrifice","sac","sacrifice area","sacrifice bunt","sacrifice fly","sacrifice hit","sacrificeless","sacrifice zone","salary sacrifice","self-sacrifice","supreme sacrifice","ultimate sacrifice","resacrifice"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sacrifice#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:993deb4fd529190096","definition":"The offering of devotion, penitence, prayer, thanksgiving, etc., to a deity.","example":"Let vs therfore by him [Jesus] offre allwayes vnto God the ſacrifice of prayſe: that is to ſaye, the frute of thoſe lippes which confeſſe his name.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"countable, figuratively, uncountable","wordFamily":["human sacrifice","nonsacrifice","presacrifice","pseudosacrifice","sac","sacrifice area","sacrifice bunt","sacrifice fly","sacrifice hit","sacrificeless","sacrifice zone","salary sacrifice","self-sacrifice","supreme sacrifice","ultimate sacrifice","resacrifice"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sacrifice#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3557bbc4a427460587","definition":"Jesus Christ's voluntary offering of himself to God the Father to be crucified as atonement for the sins of humankind.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"specifically","register":"countable, specifically, uncountable","wordFamily":["human sacrifice","nonsacrifice","presacrifice","pseudosacrifice","sac","sacrifice area","sacrifice bunt","sacrifice fly","sacrifice hit","sacrificeless","sacrifice zone","salary sacrifice","self-sacrifice","supreme sacrifice","ultimate sacrifice","resacrifice"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sacrifice#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:082e419731d05f6828","definition":"The rite of Holy Communion or the Mass, regarded as (Protestantism) an offering of thanksgiving to God for Christ's crucifixion, or (Roman Catholicism) a perpetual re-presentation of Christ's sacrificial offering.","example":"The pretensions of the holy see, the authority of tradition, purgatory, transubstantiation, the sacrifice of the mass, […] were copiously discussed.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"broadly, specifically","register":"broadly, countable, specifically, uncountable","wordFamily":["human sacrifice","nonsacrifice","presacrifice","pseudosacrifice","sac","sacrifice area","sacrifice bunt","sacrifice fly","sacrifice hit","sacrificeless","sacrifice zone","salary sacrifice","self-sacrifice","supreme sacrifice","ultimate sacrifice","resacrifice"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sacrifice#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:796666933b13702abe","definition":"The destruction or surrender of anything for the sake of something else regarded as more urgent or valuable; also, the thing destroyed or surrendered for this purpose.","example":"the sacrifice of one’s spare time in order to volunteer","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"countable, figuratively, uncountable","wordFamily":["human sacrifice","nonsacrifice","presacrifice","pseudosacrifice","sac","sacrifice area","sacrifice bunt","sacrifice fly","sacrifice hit","sacrificeless","sacrifice zone","salary sacrifice","self-sacrifice","supreme sacrifice","ultimate sacrifice","resacrifice"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sacrifice#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ec828b7f4a8c5183f3","definition":"Ellipsis of sacrifice bunt or sacrifice hit (“a play in which the batter intentionally hits the ball softly with a hands-spread batting stance at the cost of an out to advance one or more runners”).","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"abbreviation, alt-of, ellipsis, figuratively","register":"abbreviation, alt-of, countable, ellipsis, figuratively, uncountable","wordFamily":["human sacrifice","nonsacrifice","presacrifice","pseudosacrifice","sac","sacrifice area","sacrifice bunt","sacrifice fly","sacrifice hit","sacrificeless","sacrifice zone","salary sacrifice","self-sacrifice","supreme sacrifice","ultimate sacrifice","resacrifice"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sacrifice#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:add75488ca73dcdc3e","definition":"In full sacrifice bid: a bid of a contract which is unlikely to be fulfilled, that a player makes in the hope that they will incur fewer penalty points than the points likely to be gained by opponents in making their contract.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":["save"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"countable, figuratively, uncountable","wordFamily":["human sacrifice","nonsacrifice","presacrifice","pseudosacrifice","sac","sacrifice area","sacrifice bunt","sacrifice fly","sacrifice hit","sacrificeless","sacrifice zone","salary sacrifice","self-sacrifice","supreme sacrifice","ultimate sacrifice","resacrifice"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sacrifice#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:260f5b2670314f663b","definition":"A monetary loss incurred by selling something at less than its value; also, the thing thus sold.","example":"The Old Year was already looked upon as dead; and its effects were selling cheap like some drowned mariner's aboardship. Its patterns were Last Year's and going at a sacrifice, before its breath was gone. Its treasures were mere dirt, beside the riches of its unborn successor!","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"dated, figuratively, slang","register":"countable, dated, figuratively, slang, uncountable","wordFamily":["human sacrifice","nonsacrifice","presacrifice","pseudosacrifice","sac","sacrifice area","sacrifice bunt","sacrifice fly","sacrifice hit","sacrificeless","sacrifice zone","salary sacrifice","self-sacrifice","supreme sacrifice","ultimate sacrifice","resacrifice"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sacrifice#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:bd8281a0be00cc44b1","definition":"An act of intentionally allowing one's piece to be captured by the opponent in order to improve one's position in the game.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"countable, figuratively, uncountable","wordFamily":["human sacrifice","nonsacrifice","presacrifice","pseudosacrifice","sac","sacrifice area","sacrifice bunt","sacrifice fly","sacrifice hit","sacrificeless","sacrifice zone","salary sacrifice","self-sacrifice","supreme sacrifice","ultimate sacrifice","resacrifice"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sacrifice#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:93877e19cc0d2f0a8e","definition":"To offer (a human being or an animal, or an object) to a deity.","example":"And there ſhall bee no leauened bread ſeene with thee in all thy coaſts ſeuen dayes, neither ſhall there any thing of the fleſh, which thou ſacrificedſt the firſt day at Euen, remaine all night, vntill the morning.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["Molochise","Molochize"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["human sacrifice","nonsacrifice","presacrifice","pseudosacrifice","sac","sacrifice area","sacrifice bunt","sacrifice fly","sacrifice hit","sacrificeless","sacrifice zone","salary sacrifice","self-sacrifice","supreme sacrifice","ultimate sacrifice","resacrifice","sacrificable",