rifice","supreme sacrifice","ultimate sacrifice","resacrifice","sacrificable","sacrificeable","sacrificed","sacrificer","sacrificing","sacrificingly","self-sacrificing","unsacrificeable","unsacrificed","unsacrificing"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sacrifice#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c2557ebf5a98319983","definition":"Of a batter: to advance (one or more runners on base) by batting the ball so it can be fielded, placing the batter out but with insufficient time to put the runner(s) out.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"broadly, figuratively","register":"broadly, figuratively, transitive","wordFamily":["human sacrifice","nonsacrifice","presacrifice","pseudosacrifice","sac","sacrifice area","sacrifice bunt","sacrifice fly","sacrifice hit","sacrificeless","sacrifice zone","salary sacrifice","self-sacrifice","supreme sacrifice","ultimate sacrifice","resacrifice","sacrificable","sacrificeable","sacrificed","sacrificer","sacrificing","sacrificingly","self-sacrificing","unsacrificeable","unsacrificed","unsacrificing"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sacrifice#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:306c53f61bbbdef7d7","definition":"To sell (something) at less than its value, thus incurring a monetary loss.","example":"A newspaper advertisement announces that \"A professional gentleman is instructed to sacrifice Three young sound Horses at half their cost.\" We wonder what deity horses could be sacrificed to?","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"broadly, dated, figuratively, slang","register":"broadly, dated, figuratively, slang, transitive","wordFamily":["human sacrifice","nonsacrifice","presacrifice","pseudosacrifice","sac","sacrifice area","sacrifice bunt","sacrifice fly","sacrifice hit","sacrificeless","sacrifice zone","salary sacrifice","self-sacrifice","supreme sacrifice","ultimate sacrifice","resacrifice","sacrificable","sacrificeable","sacrificed","sacrificer","sacrificing","sacrificingly","self-sacrificing","unsacrificeable","unsacrificed","unsacrificing"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sacrifice#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:bb67abc5bd5e4ac012","definition":"To intentionally allow (a piece) to be captured by the opponent in order to improve one's position in the game.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"broadly, figuratively","register":"broadly, figuratively, transitive","wordFamily":["human sacrifice","nonsacrifice","presacrifice","pseudosacrifice","sac","sacrifice area","sacrifice bunt","sacrifice fly","sacrifice hit","sacrificeless","sacrifice zone","salary sacrifice","self-sacrifice","supreme sacrifice","ultimate sacrifice","resacrifice","sacrificable","sacrificeable","sacrificed","sacrificer","sacrificing","sacrificingly","self-sacrificing","unsacrificeable","unsacrificed","unsacrificing"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sacrifice#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3b7149933d86569181","definition":"To offer a human being or an animal, or an object, to a deity.","example":"All things come alike to all: there is one euent to the righteous and to the wicked, to the good and to the cleane, and to the vncleane; to him that ſacrificeth, and to him that ſacrificeth not: as is the good, ſo is the ſinner, and hee that ſweareth, as he that feareth an oath.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["human sacrifice","nonsacrifice","presacrifice","pseudosacrifi